Vendored: Sources/SwiftTerm/** from the tag above, minus:
  - Sources/SwiftTerm/iOS/**            (iOS only; Orion is macOS only)
  - Sources/SwiftTerm/Documentation.docc/** (docs, not code)
  - Sources/SwiftTerm/Mac/README.md     (docs, not code)
  - Sources/SwiftTerm/Apple/Metal/Shaders.metal
    (needs a compiled .metallib as a package resource, which swiftc-direct
    builds have no pipeline for; MetalTerminalRenderer's
    `device.makeDefaultLibrary()` returns nil without it and the view falls
    back to its CoreGraphics/CoreText renderer, so Orion's terminal draws
    without a GPU path rather than failing to build)

One symbol renamed from upstream: `Colors.swift`'s top-level `public class
Color` is `TermColor` here (and every unqualified reference to it, in
Colors.swift, Apple/AppleTerminalView.swift, Apple/ColorBridge.swift,
Mac/MacExtensions.swift and Terminal.swift — `Attribute.Color`, the
*nested* per-cell color enum in CharData.swift, is untouched, it never
collided). Orion compiles this library straight into the app's own module
(no separate SwiftPM module boundary), so SwiftTerm's top-level `Color`
and `SwiftUI.Color` become two same-named module-scope types; the compiler
resolves that ambiguity inconsistently by call site rather than rejecting
it outright, which broke `Palette.line`-style SwiftUI color usage in
AssistantPanel.swift with no error anywhere else. Renaming the vendored
class is the permanent fix — qualifying call sites in Orion's own files
would only paper over the next file that hits it.

Plus one generated file, checked in because Orion builds with swiftc
directly rather than through SwiftPM's plugin pipeline:
  - Sources/SwiftTerm/SwiftTermBuildInfo.swift
    Produced by running the tag's own
    Sources/SwiftTermBuildInfoGenerator/BuildInfoGenerator.swift against this
    checkout (that generator is normally invoked by
    Plugins/SwiftTermBuildInfoPlugin at SwiftPM build time). Only
    `Terminal.swift`'s XTVERSION (DECRQSS) reply reads it; regenerate the
    same way after re-vendoring a newer tag.

Re-vendor: `git clone --depth 1 --branch <tag> https://github.com/migueldeicaza/SwiftTerm`,
rsync Sources/SwiftTerm/ over this directory with the excludes above, then
re-run BuildInfoGenerator as described and bump the tag/commit here.

Local change: Buffer.dump() (no callers) writes to the temporary directory, not
upstream's hardcoded /Users/<author>/Downloads/Logs, so no home path is compiled
into Orion (DECISIONS #266).
